From 2c467f4f9d89eccd2584b29fb3e516de0b44858e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: platform <platform@system.local>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 11:27:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mm: one sign-in with the boards (accept mm's gateway
 assertion)

Behind mm's sign-in gateway, Doop opens a second listener (MM_GATEWAY_PORT,
4401) for its public host. Every request and WebSocket upgrade there needs
the gateway's X-Mm-Assertion: base64url(JSON {u, r, h, exp, n}) "." an
Ed25519 signature, checked with the gateway's public key
(MM_GATEWAY_PUBLIC_KEY_FILE or MM_GATEWAY_PUBLIC_KEY), for MM_GATEWAY_HOST,
not expired, a known role and name.

- The person's Doop account is made on their first visit (linked by an
  mm-gateway account row, never by email; the gateway's email domain is
  refused to Doop's own sign-up). The request runs as a server-side session
  of that account: the client's Cookie and Authorization are dropped and no
  Set-Cookie leaves, so there is no second login and nothing outlives the
  gateway's say-so.
- Doop's own sign-in, sign-up and account routes are off there (only
  GET /api/auth/get-session passes).
- owner and designer edit every canvas of this Doop; member and viewer only
  look (GET/HEAD, every canvas at 'view'); rooms of someone with no fresh
  assertion close after 10 minutes.
- Doop's own listener (PORT) is unchanged. Without a gateway key there is
  no second listener and Doop behaves as before.
